<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portuguese one-year bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portuguese one-year bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield rose to 5.9794 percent, from 5.8636 percent previously, at the Institute for Public Credit Management's sale of 364-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Institute placed 12.9 billion escudos of the 20 billion on offer. The last such sale was on March 12.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
